1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Threatened by a ruthless demon, humanity was on the brink of destruction.

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:16,000
All seemed lost until a lone mage stepped forward and took up the fight.

3
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:29,000
After his triumph, he was hailed as the Wizard King, and his story became legend.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,000
To be continued...

5
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Flame creation magic, Leo Ruggians!

6
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Ah, is that all you've got?

7
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:53,000
I had to say, Captain, I'm very disappointed in you!

8
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:10,000
When you attacked, the mana grew thin in some places across the barrier for the briefest moment. Those were the spots I aimed for.

9
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:13,000
Man! He's awesome!

10
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Listen to me, Radies. You have incredible talent, as well as powerful magic. But wielded without a just spirit, they are no more than savagery.

11
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:29,000
You're a monster! They were right to have expelled you!

12
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:35,000
I need to get stronger, so I can handle something like this more easily.

13
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:42,000
It's a bit early to be celebrating. The preparations must be nearly complete by now.

14
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:49,000
Time for a feast. Such lively young mana. Absolutely delicious.

15
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:51,000
Part 2

16
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:54,000
action for a while.

17
00:01:54,000 --> 00:02:00,000
yearn

18
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:29,980
Thank you.

19
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:59,980
Thank you.

20
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:02,000
Thank you.

21
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:42,100
I've honed my magic, studied the enemy, made meticulous preparations, years of work, countless hours of planning for this day, for this moment.

22
00:03:42,100 --> 00:03:46,040
All wasted.

23
00:03:46,720 --> 00:03:48,040
How did this happen?

24
00:03:48,040 --> 00:04:10,220
Nice work. Thanks for the shield.

25
00:04:10,220 --> 00:04:12,480
Keep your thanks and take care of him already.

26
00:04:13,100 --> 00:04:13,820
I'm on it.

27
00:04:20,220 --> 00:04:22,580
Flame magic! Viral flame!

28
00:04:22,580 --> 00:04:44,020
It's over!

29
00:04:44,020 --> 00:04:46,840
Sir, that pile of ash won't give us any trouble now!

30
00:04:50,120 --> 00:04:51,920
Very well done, both of you.

31
00:04:52,160 --> 00:04:55,240
You've shown your worth as magic knights and as royalties.

32
00:04:55,360 --> 00:04:55,700
Sir!

33
00:04:55,700 --> 00:04:58,860
What am I doing saluting him?

34
00:05:02,700 --> 00:05:04,420
No. Impossible!

35
00:05:06,420 --> 00:05:10,820
I'm stronger! Royalty or not, nobody is more powerful than I am!

36
00:05:11,080 --> 00:05:11,880
You'll see!

37
00:05:11,880 --> 00:05:15,760
Now, flame creation magic, Leo Palma.

38
00:05:21,760 --> 00:05:24,160
Get these flames off of me, damn you!

39
00:05:24,380 --> 00:05:25,540
This isn't fair!

40
00:05:25,940 --> 00:05:26,840
It's not over!

41
00:05:27,200 --> 00:05:28,120
I'll show you!

42
00:05:28,900 --> 00:05:29,340
Free me, don't prove how powerful I am!

43
00:05:29,340 --> 00:05:31,840
There are a great many questions I would like to ask.

44
00:05:31,840 --> 00:05:34,460
And you will answer.

45
00:05:34,920 --> 00:05:37,280
But first, I'm going to take a look at your grimoire.

46
00:05:38,080 --> 00:05:39,280
Wait! No!

47
00:05:41,700 --> 00:05:43,440
That's mine! Don't touch it!

48
00:05:43,720 --> 00:05:44,840
You have no right!

49
00:05:46,120 --> 00:05:46,640
Interesting.

50
00:05:47,400 --> 00:05:49,060
It seems unusually thin.

51
00:05:49,200 --> 00:05:50,660
No! Leave it alone!

52
00:05:54,360 --> 00:05:54,880
Unbelievable.

53
00:05:55,660 --> 00:05:57,380
It only has one page.

54
00:05:57,800 --> 00:05:58,660
Quit looking!

55
00:05:59,180 --> 00:06:00,520
Put it down now!

56
00:06:00,520 --> 00:06:01,560
One page?

57
00:06:01,560 --> 00:06:02,340
That's mine!

58
00:06:02,440 --> 00:06:04,640
Does this mean he can only wield a single spell?

59
00:06:05,700 --> 00:06:06,800
Give it back!

60
00:06:07,300 --> 00:06:08,480
Haven't you done enough?

61
00:06:08,800 --> 00:06:10,780
I don't need your mockery, too!

62
00:06:11,040 --> 00:06:11,560
Mockery?

63
00:06:11,800 --> 00:06:13,380
I don't hear anyone laughing!

64
00:06:18,500 --> 00:06:21,240
I get that you wanted people to take you seriously.

65
00:06:21,860 --> 00:06:24,360
But I don't understand why you had to do it like this.

66
00:06:25,920 --> 00:06:26,920
You're strong.

67
00:06:27,540 --> 00:06:29,320
And you've got a ton of magic power.

68
00:06:29,320 --> 00:06:32,880
But now, all that strength and power mean nothing!

69
00:06:32,880 --> 00:06:34,800
You threw them away!

70
00:06:34,800 --> 00:06:34,820
You threw them away!

71
00:06:41,620 --> 00:06:42,420
Come here.

72
00:06:42,660 --> 00:06:44,100
I try not to get me all dirty.

73
00:06:44,600 --> 00:06:45,040
Thanks.

74
00:06:45,160 --> 00:06:45,980
I'll do my best.

75
00:06:46,740 --> 00:06:50,320
Perhaps you could have become a great man if you had gone down a different path.

76
00:06:50,320 --> 00:06:53,780
This is where the lack of a just heart has led you.

77
00:06:55,040 --> 00:06:56,340
You must atone.

78
00:06:57,660 --> 00:06:58,140
Will?

79
00:06:58,500 --> 00:06:59,640
Are you satisfied?

80
00:07:00,980 --> 00:07:01,900
A voice?

81
00:07:01,900 --> 00:07:03,460
What is it?

82
00:07:03,520 --> 00:07:04,080
What's wrong?

83
00:07:04,440 --> 00:07:06,420
I hope you've at least learned a lesson.

84
00:07:07,080 --> 00:07:10,340
Clearly your might alone was not enough to defeat a squad, Captain.

85
00:07:10,340 --> 00:07:10,580
No.

86
00:07:10,800 --> 00:07:11,700
I almost won.

87
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:12,360
Really?

88
00:07:15,360 --> 00:07:18,740
Sometimes you cannot win, no matter how great your power.

89
00:07:19,380 --> 00:07:21,140
My power, too, nears its limit.

90
00:07:21,740 --> 00:07:23,340
No more acting on your own.

91
00:07:23,340 --> 00:07:27,520
From now on, we proceed according to plan.

92
00:07:27,940 --> 00:07:29,440
For the Master's sake.

93
00:07:33,640 --> 00:07:35,560
Three cheers for the magic knights!

94
00:07:36,140 --> 00:07:37,660
I knew you would save us!

95
00:07:37,800 --> 00:07:38,500
Thank you!

96
00:07:38,620 --> 00:07:42,100
Now then, I can practically hear Desert calling my name.

97
00:07:42,580 --> 00:07:43,960
Would you care to come along?

98
00:07:45,560 --> 00:07:46,440
I'll pass.

99
00:07:46,540 --> 00:07:47,000
Thank you.

100
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:55,900
A nice hot bath sounds awesome right about now, huh, Char?

101
00:07:56,540 --> 00:07:56,980
Heavenly.

102
00:07:57,720 --> 00:07:59,220
Good job, Blue Rose Knights!

103
00:07:59,440 --> 00:08:00,100
Thank you!

104
00:08:00,480 --> 00:08:02,620
Captain Charlotte is just so amazing!

105
00:08:03,260 --> 00:08:05,020
Not to mention beautiful, too!

106
00:08:05,580 --> 00:08:06,900
Soul is cooler, though!

107
00:08:06,900 --> 00:08:09,700
Ha ha ha ha!

108
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:18,920
I have a feeling this isn't over.

109
00:08:19,520 --> 00:08:20,440
What do they want?

110
00:08:32,880 --> 00:08:33,400
Excellent.

111
00:08:33,900 --> 00:08:36,120
They're all in the designated areas.

112
00:08:43,440 --> 00:08:44,560
My grimoire.

113
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:49,040
Magic?

114
00:08:51,100 --> 00:08:54,820
Allow me to thank you for your service, magic knights.

115
00:08:57,920 --> 00:08:58,560
What the?

116
00:08:59,480 --> 00:09:00,200
Look out!

117
00:09:00,200 --> 00:09:24,340
Where did the magic knights go?

118
00:09:24,580 --> 00:09:26,120
They disappeared completely.

119
00:09:26,120 --> 00:09:27,160
But how?

120
00:09:27,780 --> 00:09:28,720
Soul's gone!

121
00:09:30,200 --> 00:09:48,580
Oh, heavens!

122
00:09:48,840 --> 00:09:49,720
Where are we?

123
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:55,080
I would estimate that we're at least a few hundred kilometers from the royal capital, judging by the terrain here.

124
00:09:55,080 --> 00:09:56,920
They sent us away?

125
00:09:57,300 --> 00:09:58,700
That's not nice!

126
00:09:59,380 --> 00:10:01,400
Our enemy has taken things a step further.

127
00:10:02,340 --> 00:10:06,080
I knew there was a strong spatial magic user working with them, but even so...

128
00:10:06,600 --> 00:10:10,140
To do this, transporting us all would require great skill.

129
00:10:11,520 --> 00:10:13,360
We have failed!

130
00:10:15,460 --> 00:10:16,360
Something's wrong.

131
00:10:16,940 --> 00:10:18,840
Where'd the other magic knights' mana go?

132
00:10:18,840 --> 00:10:21,060
I don't know, but I can't sense it either.

133
00:10:21,060 --> 00:10:25,480
I want to know how you carried out this attack.

134
00:10:25,920 --> 00:10:27,520
Where are the others you're working with?

135
00:10:28,360 --> 00:10:29,660
Ha ha ha.

136
00:10:30,820 --> 00:10:32,880
Um, does anyone know what's happening?

137
00:10:33,360 --> 00:10:34,920
Something is definitely wrong.

138
00:10:34,920 --> 00:10:45,640
Those idiots fell for it hook, line, and sinker.

139
00:10:45,800 --> 00:10:47,140
It was almost too easy.

140
00:10:47,480 --> 00:10:49,640
And these are the greatest mages in the country?

141
00:10:49,980 --> 00:10:51,040
How utterly pathetic.

142
00:10:52,320 --> 00:10:57,120
I was going to play with any of the knights who escaped, but I suppose I won't get to now.

143
00:10:58,180 --> 00:10:58,960
Oh well.

144
00:10:59,540 --> 00:11:01,100
This place is full of young mana.

145
00:11:01,300 --> 00:11:02,540
Time to start harvesting.

146
00:11:02,540 --> 00:11:04,620
Ash Curse Magic.

147
00:11:05,940 --> 00:11:07,880
Ash Absorbing Formation.

148
00:11:14,460 --> 00:11:15,880
What is happening?

149
00:11:21,440 --> 00:11:22,400
Much better.

150
00:11:22,820 --> 00:11:26,480
Thanks to your generous donations, I can feel myself growing younger already.

151
00:11:26,680 --> 00:11:28,580
Who knew that skin could be this smooth?

152
00:11:31,120 --> 00:11:31,600
Magic!

153
00:11:31,600 --> 00:11:33,340
Just let him go!

154
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:36,200
You think you're so sweet and cute, don't you?

155
00:11:36,320 --> 00:11:37,100
Well, you're not!

156
00:11:37,320 --> 00:11:37,760
Sal!

157
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:47,680
Eliza!

158
00:11:47,800 --> 00:11:48,180
No!

159
00:11:48,400 --> 00:11:49,000
Eliza!

160
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:49,120
Eliza!

161
00:11:50,120 --> 00:11:51,280
Oh my.

162
00:11:51,960 --> 00:11:53,800
Now there's a fine-looking specimen.

163
00:11:53,800 --> 00:11:59,520
Tell me, my dear, am I beautiful?

164
00:11:59,780 --> 00:12:01,560
Care to take a guess at my age?

165
00:12:01,720 --> 00:12:02,360
I'm waiting.

166
00:12:03,560 --> 00:12:04,560
What have you done?

167
00:12:04,820 --> 00:12:06,160
You're some kind of monster!

168
00:12:06,820 --> 00:12:08,360
No one calls me a monster!

169
00:12:08,620 --> 00:12:09,120
No one!

170
00:12:09,200 --> 00:12:09,680
No!

171
00:12:09,680 --> 00:12:09,760
No!

172
00:12:09,760 --> 00:12:10,160
No!

173
00:12:10,160 --> 00:12:10,360
No!

174
00:12:10,360 --> 00:12:10,480
No!

175
00:12:10,480 --> 00:12:10,520
No!

176
00:12:10,520 --> 00:12:10,580
No!

177
00:12:10,580 --> 00:12:11,020
No!

178
00:12:11,020 --> 00:12:11,080
No!

179
00:12:11,080 --> 00:12:11,520
No!

180
00:12:11,520 --> 00:12:11,580
No!

181
00:12:11,580 --> 00:12:12,080
No!

182
00:12:12,080 --> 00:12:12,580
No!

183
00:12:12,580 --> 00:12:12,720
No!

184
00:12:12,720 --> 00:12:13,080
No!

185
00:12:13,080 --> 00:12:13,580
No!

186
00:12:13,580 --> 00:12:14,080
No!

187
00:12:14,080 --> 00:12:14,580
No!

188
00:12:14,580 --> 00:12:15,580
No!

189
00:12:15,580 --> 00:12:16,580
No!

190
00:12:16,580 --> 00:12:17,580
No!

191
00:12:17,580 --> 00:12:18,580
No!

192
00:12:18,580 --> 00:12:19,580
No!

193
00:12:19,580 --> 00:12:20,580
No!

194
00:12:20,580 --> 00:12:21,580
No!

195
00:12:21,580 --> 00:12:22,580
No!

196
00:12:22,580 --> 00:12:23,140
No!

197
00:12:31,100 --> 00:12:31,620
Ooh!

198
00:12:31,620 --> 00:12:33,740
And lucky for me, this one's a beauty!

199
00:12:33,740 --> 00:12:37,140
What do you say we have some fun together, lovely?

200
00:12:37,140 --> 00:12:41,140
I'm not gonna let you hurt any more of these people, you old hag.

201
00:12:43,020 --> 00:12:43,820
You're dead!

202
00:12:52,580 --> 00:13:00,440
Oh, and lucky for me, this one's a beauty.

203
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:03,340
What do you say we have some fun together, lovely?

204
00:13:03,900 --> 00:13:06,340
I'm not going to let you hurt any more of these people.

205
00:13:07,280 --> 00:13:08,060
You old hag.

206
00:13:09,820 --> 00:13:10,740
You're dead!

207
00:13:11,740 --> 00:13:13,920
How dare you call me an old hag!

208
00:13:14,840 --> 00:13:16,020
Ash curse magic!

209
00:13:16,320 --> 00:13:17,680
Cheerful ash destruction!

210
00:13:17,680 --> 00:13:23,360
These little shells contain all kinds of lovely curses.

211
00:13:27,640 --> 00:13:31,060
The best part is you won't know what they'll do until they hit you.

212
00:13:34,700 --> 00:13:36,520
Who are you and why are you here?

213
00:13:37,020 --> 00:13:38,620
What are you people hoping to accomplish?

214
00:13:39,600 --> 00:13:42,160
Ah, so you have enough breath to chat, do you?

215
00:13:42,400 --> 00:13:45,480
Very well, your pretty face has earned you an answer.

216
00:13:45,480 --> 00:13:48,100
Our mission is relatively simple.

217
00:13:48,540 --> 00:13:50,660
There's a certain someone we need to get rid of.

218
00:13:50,980 --> 00:13:52,000
And who would that be?

219
00:13:52,440 --> 00:13:55,240
Oh, come now, you don't honestly think I would tell you.

220
00:13:58,400 --> 00:14:01,280
Right, good looks only gets you so far!

221
00:14:05,080 --> 00:14:08,020
There's at least one other involved in this plot besides you.

222
00:14:08,560 --> 00:14:11,860
This invasion required the use of spatial magic on an immense scale.

223
00:14:12,520 --> 00:14:13,960
So tell me, where is your partner?

224
00:14:13,960 --> 00:14:17,860
Have they escaped already?

225
00:14:19,360 --> 00:14:22,460
They may have managed to send the magic knights away from the capital,

226
00:14:22,820 --> 00:14:25,680
but that doesn't mean they have the power necessary to capture it.

227
00:14:27,200 --> 00:14:30,580
Nor do I believe this to be something as simple as a feint to reach the king.

228
00:14:30,580 --> 00:14:44,780
You've made it clear your personal motive is revenge,

229
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:47,740
but I sense that there was a larger purpose behind the attack.

230
00:14:47,740 --> 00:14:58,600
Do you want to know what we're after?

231
00:14:59,600 --> 00:15:03,120
You, Fregolian Vermillion, we came for you!

232
00:15:03,340 --> 00:15:03,840
For me.

233
00:15:03,840 --> 00:15:07,520
But why him?

234
00:15:08,200 --> 00:15:09,000
Yes, why?

235
00:15:13,380 --> 00:15:14,900
Spatial magic again, eh?

236
00:15:15,700 --> 00:15:16,520
Very well.

237
00:15:16,940 --> 00:15:18,740
Maybe now we'll get to the bottom of this.

238
00:15:18,740 --> 00:15:30,840
Strange, what is this place?

239
00:15:30,840 --> 00:15:30,860
Strange, what is this place?

240
00:15:30,860 --> 00:15:56,580
Strange, what is this place?

241
00:15:56,580 --> 00:16:01,980
Her attacks just keep coming, and she isn't tiring at all.

242
00:16:02,740 --> 00:16:06,580
The shells themselves don't do much damage, but what's inside them...

243
00:16:06,580 --> 00:16:11,140
Oh dear, look at you flail.

244
00:16:11,720 --> 00:16:14,440
Which of my curses has its grip on you now, I wonder?

245
00:16:14,840 --> 00:16:16,820
You don't seem to be so chatty anymore.

246
00:16:17,520 --> 00:16:18,740
Damn you.

247
00:16:20,440 --> 00:16:23,320
My eyes, I can barely see now.

248
00:16:24,160 --> 00:16:25,680
It's not just my vision.

249
00:16:25,680 --> 00:16:27,900
All of my senses are fading.

250
00:16:28,400 --> 00:16:30,240
Say, can you hear me?

251
00:16:30,780 --> 00:16:31,300
Hello?

252
00:16:33,720 --> 00:16:35,660
My hearing's almost gone now.

253
00:16:36,300 --> 00:16:38,060
What kind of power does this woman have?

254
00:16:38,740 --> 00:16:41,520
Are you enjoying my cheerful ash destruction spell?

255
00:16:41,800 --> 00:16:43,620
It works slowly, but quite effectively.

256
00:16:44,060 --> 00:16:45,500
It looks like you've lost your vision.

257
00:16:45,900 --> 00:16:47,460
And your hearing too, I would guess.

258
00:16:47,680 --> 00:16:49,360
Soon you won't even be able to move.

259
00:16:50,700 --> 00:16:53,200
Sensory deprivation and the fear that comes with it.

260
00:16:53,200 --> 00:16:55,760
That's your punishment for calling me an old hag.

261
00:16:55,760 --> 00:16:59,540
The four-leaf clover.

262
00:16:59,540 --> 00:17:05,080
However, I joined the Golden Dawn to live up to the expectations that came with this grimoire.

263
00:17:06,400 --> 00:17:09,620
But what happens if I never can?

264
00:17:10,420 --> 00:17:13,380
Four-leaf clover or not, you're still just a commoner.

265
00:17:13,760 --> 00:17:14,660
Don't get cocky.

266
00:17:14,660 --> 00:17:18,880
Your skills merit little attention in the Golden Dawn, village boy.

267
00:17:19,500 --> 00:17:22,080
Soon enough, no one will remember your name.

268
00:17:22,600 --> 00:17:24,500
I ignored the people who doubted me.

269
00:17:25,540 --> 00:17:29,160
Instead, I honed my skills and worked to make myself unbeatable.

270
00:17:30,060 --> 00:17:31,380
Except...

271
00:17:31,380 --> 00:17:32,500
I couldn't win.

272
00:17:33,320 --> 00:17:35,180
It wasn't me who defeated him.

273
00:17:35,960 --> 00:17:38,120
It was a power buried in that dungeon.

274
00:17:39,240 --> 00:17:41,280
When I just happened to stumble across.

275
00:17:42,500 --> 00:17:44,060
A power I can't control.

276
00:17:45,160 --> 00:17:48,180
